From: Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:03:48 +0100
Subject: sctp: patch over auth_hmacs copy overflow
Patch-mainline: Never, CVE-2026-68376 workaround
References: CVE-2026-68376 bsc#1274836

Because we can't get e0b5252a59383b77d1b8dbeda00b7184dd95f4d3 without
breaking kABI, simply error out in sctp_association_init() if the hmacs
list is too long.

Signed-off-by: Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>
---
 net/sctp/associola.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/sctp/associola.c b/net/sctp/associola.c
index 099b636d47cf..9803c011c616 100644
--- a/net/sctp/associola.c
+++ b/net/sctp/associola.c
@@ -318,6 +318,14 @@ static struct sctp_association *sctp_association_init(struct sctp_association *a
 
 	/* AUTH related initializations */
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&asoc->endpoint_shared_keys);
+
+	if (ep->auth_hmacs_list) {
+		if (ntohs(ep->auth_hmacs_list->param_hdr.length) >
+			  sizeof(asoc->c.auth_hmacs)) {
+			pr_warn_once("sctp: hmacs list too long\n");
+			goto fail_init;
+		}
+	}
 	err = sctp_auth_asoc_copy_shkeys(ep, asoc, gfp);
 	if (err)
 		goto fail_init;

